CCAAVVEEAATTSS
     It is easy to shoot yourself in the foot by setting fail points too ag‐
     gressively or setting too many in combination.  For example, forcing
     mmaalllloocc() to fail consistently is potentially harmful to uptime.

     The sslleeeepp() sysctl setting may not be appropriate in all situations.
     Currently, ffaaiill__ppooiinntt__eevvaall() does not verify whether the context is ap‐
     propriate for calling mmsslleeeepp().  You can force it to evaluate a sslleeeepp ac‐
     tion as a ddeellaayy action by specifying the FFAAIILL__PPOOIINNTT__NNOONNSSLLEEEEPPAABBLLEE flag at
     the point the fail point is declared.

